1
00:00:32,100 --> 00:00:33,478
I was here first!

2
00:00:33,480 --> 00:00:34,538
Since when?

3
00:00:34,540 --> 00:00:35,808
Since breakfast!

4
00:00:45,600 --> 00:00:48,145
Captain says it's too hot to fly.

5
00:00:49,108 --> 00:00:50,947
Pigeons don't say things.

6
00:01:38,542 --> 00:01:39,891
Khadoos Uncle.

7
00:01:41,133 --> 00:01:43,334
He wears a cardigan. In June.

8
00:01:43,983 --> 00:01:46,182
Maybe he's cold inside.

9
00:02:07,133 --> 00:02:09,066
Captain! You're not allowed!

10
00:03:20,900 --> 00:03:21,865
Whoa.

11
00:03:31,800 --> 00:03:33,870
WHO is on my roof?

12
00:03:39,525 --> 00:03:42,013
Ishaan, we are going to be in so much—

13
00:03:42,350 --> 00:03:43,346
...trouble.

14
00:04:00,550 --> 00:04:01,534
Out.

15
00:04:03,258 --> 00:04:04,632
You made a cloud.

16
00:04:05,658 --> 00:04:06,642
Out.

17
00:04:08,342 --> 00:04:09,694
You MADE a CLOUD.

18
00:04:51,750 --> 00:04:55,426
You touch nothing. You do exactly as I say.

19
00:05:01,758 --> 00:05:03,102
What are the rules?

20
00:05:04,542 --> 00:05:06,469
That was the rules.

21
00:06:31,125 --> 00:06:32,513
This is... the weather?

22
00:06:33,917 --> 00:06:37,479
The weather of Delhi. Somebody has to keep it.

23
00:06:38,342 --> 00:06:39,235
Who?

24
00:06:46,217 --> 00:06:47,773
Start sweeping.

25
00:08:06,617 --> 00:08:07,894
Hm.

26
00:08:31,517 --> 00:08:36,564
Slowly. Slowly. You are spinning a cloud, not bowling a bouncer.

27
00:08:44,708 --> 00:08:45,841
Oh no.

28
00:09:12,517 --> 00:09:15,523
Captain says that was the best day of his life.

29
00:09:55,583 --> 00:09:57,891
The monsoon's late. It's very late.

30
00:10:27,650 --> 00:10:29,288
It needs three.

31
00:10:36,025 --> 00:10:38,207
It always needed three.

32
00:11:12,533 --> 00:11:16,986
I'm done. I'm old. The city can manage on its own now.

33
00:11:23,317 --> 00:11:25,713
But it can't! It's too hot. People are—

34
00:11:25,600 --> 00:11:26,835
GO HOME.

35
00:12:05,892 --> 00:12:08,506
We just push the clouds in. Push them. Fast.

36
00:12:10,267 --> 00:12:12,412
We need wind. A lot of wind.

37
00:12:29,642 --> 00:12:31,082
Uncle said never—

38
00:12:30,892 --> 00:12:32,145
He's not here.

39
00:13:26,317 --> 00:13:27,346
BHAAP!

40
00:14:09,942 --> 00:14:10,910
Uncle?

41
00:14:13,633 --> 00:14:16,301
Just... tired. Very... tired.

42
00:14:27,258 --> 00:14:29,013
Those kids were on the roof!

43
00:14:29,458 --> 00:14:31,010
I SAW them!

44
00:15:30,650 --> 00:15:31,653
Bhaap.

45
00:15:47,008 --> 00:15:48,788
I'm sorry. About the trunk.

46
00:15:49,608 --> 00:15:51,379
I'm sorry about my plan.

47
00:15:52,208 --> 00:15:54,581
Bhaap says the trunk needs three.

48
00:16:12,433 --> 00:16:16,364
We don't ask for anything. Not ice cream, not thank you. Nothing.

49
00:16:18,433 --> 00:16:19,406
Nothing.

50
00:16:19,833 --> 00:16:20,960
Nothing.

51
00:16:39,583 --> 00:16:41,685
You can't walk it over. Throw it!

52
00:16:41,983 --> 00:16:43,561
It's a key, not a ball!

53
00:16:43,683 --> 00:16:44,939
Then bowl it!

54
00:17:05,325 --> 00:17:06,884
Now. All together.

55
00:19:05,225 --> 00:19:06,863
It needs three.

56
00:19:41,308 --> 00:19:43,098
Morning, Meghnath Uncle!
